  "interpretation": [
    "Both original indexed source meshes have 168 two-face edges with opposite directions and no boundary/overincident edges. This alone does not certify embedded intersections, vertex manifoldness or outward normals.",
    "Canonical triangle soup uses arbitrary S3 corner ordering; exactly half of each parent faces have odd relative permutations. Its induced directed shared edges are not consistent.",
    "NativeTrainingStream only adds CYCLIC rotations and a face permutation. These preserve archive orientation signs.",
    "For directed-edge cancellation distinguish original source winding from actual archive winding. For a permutation-invariant formula test the full quantity instead of inferring failure from edge-direction counts.",
    "GT source winding and corner identity are supervision/oracle labels, not inference inputs or nearest-prediction assignments."
  ],
  "recovery_algorithm": [
    "Let c=sample.source_face_ids[slot], the canonical face index.",
    "raw_corner_ids = source_raw_faces[canonical_to_raw_face[c]].",
    "archive_corner_to_raw_corner[c] uniquely satisfies raw_corner_ids[perm] == archive_source_face_vertex_ids[c].",
    "For an augmented sample compose perm_total = archive_corner_to_raw_corner[c][sample.corner_permutations[slot]].",
    "Source-oriented normal = parity(perm_total)*sample ordered-corner normal. Alternatively invert the ID-proven corner permutation for the labels-only CPU oracle. source_face_ids already tracks face permutations.",
    "Coordinates are unchanged; the raw/original CPU variant only reorders each face three FP32 corners."
  ],
